-setup","content":"When using **ox\\_core**, usable items are handled through **ox\\_inventory** item definitions rather than the framework itself. For each lootbox case item, you need to add a `server.export` entry in your ox\\_inventory item definitions that points back to this resource."},"1191":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-21","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"Add your lootbox case items to `ox_inventory/data/items.lua`:"},"1192":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-22","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"The `server.export` value **must** follow the format `sleepless_lootbox.<item_name>`, where `<item_name>` matches the lootbox key defined in your `config.lua` or registered via exports. Without this, using the item will do nothing."},"1193":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-23","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"ox\\_inventory sees that the item has a `server.export` defined."},"1194":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-24","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"When a player uses the item, ox\\_inventory calls the matching export on `sleepless_lootbox`."},"1195":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-25","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"The ox framework bridge registers these exports automatically when `config.registerUsableItems = true`."},"1196":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-26","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"The lootbox opens for the player."},"1197":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-27","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Here are all three default lootbox cases configured for ox\\_inventory:"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-28","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Don't forget to also add item definitions for any **loot contents** (weapons, items, etc.) that your lootboxes can reward. Those items don't need `server.export` — only the case items do."},"1199":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-29","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order","content":"Make sure your `server.cfg` starts resources in the correct order:"},"1200":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-30","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#qbcore--qbox-setup","content":"When using **QBCore** or **Qbox**, lootbox case items must be defined in your shared items table with `useable = true`. This allows the framework to register usable item callbacks."},"1201":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-31","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"Add your lootbox case items to `qb-core/shared/items.lua`:"},"1202":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-32","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"The `useable = true` flag is **required**. Without it, `QBCore.Functions.CreateUseableItem` (or `exports.qbx_core:CreateUseableItem` for Qbox) will not be able to register the callback, and using the item will do nothing."},"1203":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-33","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"The framework sees that the item has `useable = true` in the shared items table."},"1204":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-34","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"When `config.registerUsableItems = true`, the bridge calls `CreateUseableItem` for each lootbox."},"1205":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-35","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"When a player uses the item, the framework triggers the registered callback."},"1206":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-36","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"The lootbox opens for the player."},"1207":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-37","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example-1","content":"Here are all three default lootbox cases configured for QBCore/Qbox:"},"1208":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-38","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example-1","content":"Don't forget to also add item definitions for any **loot contents** (weapons, items, etc.) that your lootboxes can reward. Those items don't need `useable = true` — only the case items do."},"1209":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-39","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order-1","content":"Make sure your `server.cfg` starts resources in the correct order:"},"1210":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-40","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order-1","content":"For Qbox, replace `qb-core` with `qbx_core`:"},"1211":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-41","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#reference-file","content":"The resource includes a `_items.lua` reference file in its root directory containing example item definitions for both ox\\_inventory and QBCore/Qbox. This file is **not loaded at runtime** — it's purely for reference. Copy the relevant entries into your framework's item configuration."},"1212":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-42","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#adding-custom-lootboxes","content":"When you register a new lootbox (either in `config.lua` or via the `registerLootbox` export), you need to add a matching item definition to your framework:"},"1213":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-43","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**ox\\_inventory:** Verify the item definition includes `server.export = \"sleepless_lootbox.<item_name>\"` and that the item name matches your lootbox key exactly."},"1214":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-44","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**QBCore/Qbox:** Verify the item definition has `useable = true` in the shared items table."},"1215":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-45","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**All frameworks:** Ensure `config.registerUsableItems = true` in your `config.lua`."},"1216":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-46","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**All frameworks:** Ensure `sleepless_lootbox` starts **after** your framework and inventory in `server.cfg`."},"1217":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-47","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#no-supported-framework-detected-warning","content":"Check that your framework resource is started before `sleepless_lootbox`. The bridge auto-detects the framework by checking if the resource is started, so load order matters."},"1218":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-48","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#lootbox-opens-but-no-item-is-given","content":"This is likely an inventory bridge issue. Make sure the loot content items (not the case items) are also defined in your inventory system. The resource can only give items that your inventory recognizes."},"1219":{"id":"/docs/lootbox","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"page","content":"Sleepless Lootbox","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Free Resources","Lootbox"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox"},"1220":{"id":"/docs/lootbox-0","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox#features","content":"Features"},"1221":{"id":"/docs/lootbox-1","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox#dependencies","content":"Dependencies"},"1222":{"id":"/docs/lootbox-2","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox#installation","content":"Installation"},"1223":{"id":"/docs/lootbox-3","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox#download-the-resource-step","content":"Download the Resource"},"1224":{"id":"/docs/lootbox-4","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox#add-to-server-step","content":"Add to Server"},"1225":{"id":"/docs/lootbox-5","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox#configure-your-server-step","content":"Configure Your Server"},"1226":{"id":"/docs/lootbox